8. Network  hub

Your network interfaces, their addresses, where traffic goes, and how names
become addresses.

On your machine
  docker0   down · virtual · MAC 02:42:5c:11:aa:01
            172.17.0.1/16
  enp0s31f6 down · MAC 54:e1:ad:12:34:56
  lo        unknown · loopback
            127.0.0.1/8, ::1/128
  wlp0s20f3 up · wireless · MAC 8c:c6:81:2a:10:7f
            192.168.1.23/24, fe80::8ec6:81ff:fe2a:107f/64
  Route     default via 192.168.1.1 on wlp0s20f3

Commands
  ip -br addr            each interface and its addresses, one line each
  ip route               where packets go, default gateway included
  ping -c 3 example.com  is a host reachable, and how fast
  ss -tulpn              ports open for connections
  resolvectl status      DNS servers in use, per interface
  nmcli device           NetworkManager's view, Wi-Fi included
  curl -I https://example.com
                         test an HTTPS connection, headers only

Paths
  /etc/hosts        names resolved without DNS
  /etc/resolv.conf  DNS servers the system resolver asks
  /sys/class/net/   one folder per interface: state, MAC, speed

Cards
  idk 8.1  Who listens on which port
  idk 8.2  DNS resolution
  idk 8.3  Interfaces and routes
  idk 8.4  nftables vs iptables vs ufw
